place a hooded figure at (46, 54): Its empty hands are held as if about a hilt that is not there. Letters are cut deep into the plinth, in the old tongue: LĪF ÆR DĒAÞE. Below, in a later hand: 'Life before death. So the hunters swore, to the one who waited for them on the road; and the road gave them each a blade.'

